  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09TY">Exercise <span data-tag="09TY">111.56.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $S \subset A$ be a multiplicative subset. Assume that $A \to B$ is of finite type and $S^{-1}A \to S^{-1}B$ is surjective. Show that there exists an $f \in S$ such that $A_ f \to B_ f$ is surjective. </p>
